#==============================================================================#
# Whitelist .gitignore: ignore everything, then re-admit the tracked set.
#
# This repo carries the build script, the README, the data/ folder skeleton, and
# the small derived outputs -- nothing else. The research-template AI
# infrastructure (Infrastructure/, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, PROJECT.md, Makefile,
# .claude/, .codex/, .agents/) stays local, as do the raw inputs, which are
# hosted separately: see README.md for how to obtain them.
#
# To track a new file you must un-ignore it explicitly below. That is the point:
# data/raw/cps/ holds 1.2 GB Stata extracts and GitHub rejects any file over
# 100 MB, so nothing gets committed here by accident.
#==============================================================================#

# 1. Ignore every file.
*

# 2. But descend into directories, so the re-admits below can be reached.
!*/

# 3. Re-admit the tracked set.
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md

# build script
!/code/0_config.do
!/code/01_build_cps_exposure.do

# folder skeleton under data/ -- the pipeline writes into these, so a fresh
# clone needs them to exist before it can run
!/data/**/.gitkeep

# derived outputs (small; regenerable from code/01_build_cps_exposure.do)
!/data/processed/ai_exposure_cps.dta
!/data/processed/ai_exposure_cps.csv
!/data/processed/ai_exposure_occ2010.dta

# 4. Belt and braces -- never tracked, whatever else changes above.
.DS_Store

# Stray empty repo GitHub Desktop created inside this one (safe to delete).
# Named explicitly because git treats an embedded repo as a submodule-shaped
# entry that rule 2 would otherwise let through.
/ai-cps-exposure/
